We cannot confirm 3.0 MW of available capacity on Feeder ALN-108. The May 15,=
 2024 Hosting Capacity Map showed 3.0 MW for the Elderpine 13.2 kV pure-gener=
ation feeder at publication, based on the April 2024 study. Our October 15, 2=
024 interim planning update reduced the working figure to 1.8 MW after one 1.=
2 MW queue addition. It did not include a further 1.0 MW request received in =
February 2025.

The July 14, 2025 queue-adjusted planning estimate is 0.8 MW. Subtracting the=
 two active post-publication requests (2.2 MW total) from the 3.0 MW map base=
line leaves 0.8 MW, or 2.2 MW less than your request. This uses the capacitie=
s as filed; it is not a new study result or a revised map value. It does not =
reserve capacity, establish a queue position, or approve interconnection at a=
ny size.

The October planning update calls for a full feeder-level study for a project=
 of this size. A formal 3 MW application follows the medium-scale screening a=
nd system impact study path under DIS-01 Rev. 4. Updated load, existing gener=
ation, and thermal, voltage and protection review will determine whether the =
project can interconnect at the proposed location and what site-specific limi=
ts, upgrades or costs would apply. The records do not yet establish those con=
ditions. We have requested a priority feeder refresh; please consult Distribu=
tion Planning before finalizing sizing.

Please reply with two or three available times to meet with Distribution Plan=
ning and the DER Program Office. If available, include the site location, pro=
posed connection point, preliminary one-line diagram and inverter AC nameplat=
e and export details. June Halloway (june.halloway@alleniom.com) will coordin=
ate the earliest mutually available slot to discuss sizing, alternative conne=
ction points and the formal application path.

